    ]
  ]
,
  "purpose": "These three sequences separate the three put conflict modes and the three channel definitions. Experiment 1 distinguishes INSERT OR IGNORE (second put changes nothing) from INSERT OR REPLACE and ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE (second put changes the row). Experiment 2 distinguishes INSERT OR REPLACE from ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE under rollback: REPLACE deletes the old row and inserts a new one, so rollback restores the original row; DO UPDATE modifies the existing row, so rollback also restores the original row, but the channel counts differ because REPLACE performs a delete plus an insert while DO UPDATE performs one update. Experiment 3 distinguishes the channel definitions: changes() counts only the last direct statement, total_changes accumulates all direct changes on the main connection, and total_changes plus other total_changes includes other-connection changes. Together with the trigger instrumentation, these experiments separate all 18 family members."
}
